{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "My recent purchases help connect computers and peripherals or add specific capabilities. Streaming devices, smart speakers, and smart displays do not solve those same problems for me.",
    "The smart plug and camera assume I want home automation or monitoring, but my purchases do not indicate either need.",
    "The SD card is a practical accessory, but I have no current need for that storage format or capacity, so I would not choose it just because it is an accessory."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Buying electronics seems to have been taken as interest in a broad range of electronic devices, even when their purposes differ from my purchases.",
    "The repeated Alexa and streaming products suggest an interest in a connected-home setup that I have not expressed."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My WiFi adapter, USB expansion card, DVI cable, and USB-to-Ethernet adapter point toward specific computer connectivity needs; the connection type and compatibility matter to me.",
    "My purchases are spread over years and serve distinct practical purposes. I usually need a concrete problem to solve before I interact, rather than a loosely related gadget.",
    "My latest purchase provides wired networking through USB, which is a more relevant clue than a general interest in electronics, though it does not mean I need another identical adapter."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations interpreted my practical computer-accessory purchases as broad interest in smart-home and entertainment devices, leaving none that meets a current need."
}"}
